-- smucclaw/l4-ide#1107: named deadlines in three other places. A duty armed
-- by HENCE, a WITHIN beside an AFTER, and a WITHIN counted OF a named instant
-- are each worked out as their literal twin is. A named AFTER is not: its
-- window's deadline stays unknown (a limit, stated on the explore page).

DECLARE Actor IS ONE OF Alice, Bob
DECLARE Act IS ONE OF pay, ship

`ten days` MEANS 10
`five days` MEANS 5
`the start` MEANS 3

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Act
`then literal` MEANS
  PARTY Alice MUST pay WITHIN 3
  HENCE PARTY Bob MUST ship WITHIN 10 LEST BREACH BY Bob BECAUSE "late"

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Act
`then named` MEANS
  PARTY Alice MUST pay WITHIN 3
  HENCE PARTY Bob MUST ship WITHIN `ten days` LEST BREACH BY Bob BECAUSE "late"

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Act
`after literal` MEANS PARTY Alice MUST ship AFTER 5 WITHIN 10 LEST BREACH BY Alice BECAUSE "late"

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Act
`after named` MEANS PARTY Alice MUST ship AFTER 5 WITHIN `ten days` LEST BREACH BY Alice BECAUSE "late"

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Act
`of literal` MEANS PARTY Alice MUST ship WITHIN 5 OF 3 LEST BREACH BY Alice BECAUSE "late"

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Act
`of named` MEANS PARTY Alice MUST ship WITHIN `five days` OF `the start` LEST BREACH BY Alice BECAUSE "late"

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Act
`named after` MEANS PARTY Alice MUST ship AFTER `five days` WITHIN 10 LEST BREACH BY Alice BECAUSE "late"

#TRACE `then named` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY Alice DOES pay AT 2
